  "title": "Battles of Saratoga and surrender of Burgoyne",
  "summary": "Between 19 September and 7 October 1777, American and British forces fought at Freeman's Farm and Bemis Heights near Saratoga, New York. On 17 October General John Burgoyne's army surrendered to General Horatio Gates. The American victory helped convince France to sign a treaty of alliance with the United States.",
